.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd October 24, 2026
.Dt GROWFS 8
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm growfs
.Nd grow an oxfs to fill its partition
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl Ny
.Op Fl s Ar size
.Ar special
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
grows the oxfs on
.Ar special ,
a partition made larger
.Pq Xr gpart 8 Cm resize
or an image file, to fill it.
The file system must be unmounted and clean
.Pq Xr fsck_oxfs 8 ;
nothing in it changes but its size, and the new space is free.
.Pp
An oxfs's block bitmap lies before its data and grows with it: past the room
in the bitmap's last block, every data block in use moves further into the
partition to make way for the new bitmap blocks.
The move is not safe against a crash: power lost while it runs leaves the file
system damaged.
Without
.Fl y ,
.Nm
says so and asks first.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl N
Say what would be done; write nothing.
.It Fl y
Don't ask: grow at once.
.It Fl s Ar size
Grow to the first
.Ar size
512-byte sectors of
.Ar special ,
not all of it.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Grow the third partition of
.Pa ide0
into the free space after it, then its file system:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
gpart resize -i 3 ide0
growfs /dev/ide0p3
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr fsck_oxfs 8 ,
.Xr gpart 8 ,
.Xr newfs_oxfs 8
.Sh HISTORY
A
.Nm
command for UFS appeared in
.Fx 4.4 ;
this one, for oxfs, in OxideBSD 0.3.
.Sh BUGS
It can't shrink a file system, nor grow one that is mounted.
